{"content":[{"c":["JONATHAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Levite from Bethlehem in Judah, a descendant of Gershom, son of Moses (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.14-15","r":"1Chr.23.14-15","rawR":"1Chr.23.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.14-15","value":"1Chr.23.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 23:14-15"},"); he was a priest first to Micah in Ephraim and later to Dan’s tribe during the period of the judges (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.17.7-10","r":"Judg.17.7-10","rawR":"Judg.17.7-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.17.7-10","value":"Judg.17.7-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 17:7-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.18.30","r":"Judg.18.30","rawR":"Judg.18.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.18.30","value":"Judg.18.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:30"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Benjamite, the firstborn son of Saul and the father of Meribbaal (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.14.49","r":"1Sam.14.49","rawR":"1Sam.14.49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.14.49","value":"1Sam.14.49"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 14:49"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.33-34","r":"1Chr.8.33-34","rawR":"1Chr.8.33-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.33-34","value":"1Chr.8.33-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:33-34"},"). Jonathan was a valiant warrior (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.13.2-4","r":"1Sam.13.2-4","rawR":"1Sam.13.2-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.13.2-4","value":"1Sam.13.2-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 13:2-4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.14.1-15","r":"1Sam.14.1-15","rawR":"1Sam.14.1-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.14.1-15","value":"1Sam.14.1-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:1-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.1.22","r":"2Sam.1.22","rawR":"2Sam.1.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.1.22","value":"2Sam.1.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 1:22"},") and a devoted friend to David (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.18.1-5","r":"1Sam.18.1-5","rawR":"1Sam.18.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.18.1-5","value":"1Sam.18.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 18:1-5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.19.1-7","r":"1Sam.19.1-7","rawR":"1Sam.19.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.19.1-7","value":"1Sam.19.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:1-7"},"). He was eventually killed, along with his brothers, by the Philistines at Mt Gilboa (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.31.2","r":"1Sam.31.2","rawR":"1Sam.31.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.31.2","value":"1Sam.31.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 31:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.10.2","r":"1Chr.10.2","rawR":"1Chr.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.10.2","value":"1Chr.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 10:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Son of the high priest Abiathar and one of David’s loyal servants (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.15.27,36","r":"2Sam.15.27,36","rawR":"2Sam.15.27,36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.15.27,36","value":"2Sam.15.27,36"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 15:27, 36"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.17.17,20","r":"2Sam.17.17,20","rawR":"2Sam.17.17,20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.17.17,20","value":"2Sam.17.17,20"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:17, 20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.1.42-43","r":"1Kgs.1.42-43","rawR":"1Kgs.1.42-43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.1.42-43","value":"1Kgs.1.42-43"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 1:42-43"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Shimei’s son and the nephew of David (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.21","r":"2Sam.21.21","rawR":"2Sam.21.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.21","value":"2Sam.21.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 21:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.20.7","r":"1Chr.20.7","rawR":"1Chr.20.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.20.7","value":"1Chr.20.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 20:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Son of Shagee the Hararite and one of David’s mighty warriors (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.33","r":"2Sam.23.33","rawR":"2Sam.23.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.33","value":"2Sam.23.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.34","r":"1Chr.11.34","rawR":"1Chr.11.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.34","value":"1Chr.11.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:34"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. Judahite, Jada’s son, the brother of Jether, and the father of Peleth and Zaza (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.32-33","r":"1Chr.2.32-33","rawR":"1Chr.2.32-33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.32-33","value":"1Chr.2.32-33"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:32-33"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. Son of Uzziah and one of David’s treasurers (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.25","r":"1Chr.27.25","rawR":"1Chr.27.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.25","value":"1Chr.27.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. David’s relative who served as counselor and scribe in the royal household (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.32","r":"1Chr.27.32","rawR":"1Chr.27.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.32","value":"1Chr.27.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:32"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Ebed’s father. Ebed returned with Ezra to Judah following the Babylonian captivity (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.6","r":"Ezra.8.6","rawR":"Ezra.8.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.6","value":"Ezra.8.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. Asahel’s son, who, with Jahzeiah, opposed Ezra’s suggestion that the sons of Israel should divorce the foreign woman they had married since returning to Palestine from exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.15","r":"Ezra.10.15","rawR":"Ezra.10.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.15","value":"Ezra.10.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. Levite, the son of Joiada, the father of Jaddua, and a descendant of Jeshua, the high priest (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.11","r":"Neh.12.11","rawR":"Neh.12.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.11","value":"Neh.12.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:11"},"). He is perhaps the same man as Jehohanan (or Johanan), Eliashib’s grandson, in ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.6","r":"Ezra.10.6","rawR":"Ezra.10.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.6","value":"Ezra.10.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezra 10:6"}," (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.23","r":"Neh.12.23","rawR":"Neh.12.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.23","value":"Neh.12.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:23"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jehohanan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jehohanan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jehohanan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jehohanan #4"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["12. Priest and the head of Malluch’s house during the days of Joiakim the high priest (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.14","r":"Neh.12.14","rawR":"Neh.12.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.14","value":"Neh.12.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["13. Priest, father of Zechariah, and a descendant of Asaph (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.35","r":"Neh.12.35","rawR":"Neh.12.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.35","value":"Neh.12.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["14. Secretary in whose house Jeremiah was at one point imprisoned during the reign of King Zedekiah of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.37.15,20","r":"Jer.37.15,20","rawR":"Jer.37.15,20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.37.15,20","value":"Jer.37.15,20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 37:15, 20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.38.26","r":"Jer.38.26","rawR":"Jer.38.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.38.26","value":"Jer.38.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:26"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["15. Kareah’s son who sought protection under Gedaliah (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.40.8","r":"Jer.40.8","rawR":"Jer.40.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.40.8","value":"Jer.40.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 40:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["16. Youngest son of Mattathias and brother of Judas Maccabeus. When Judas Maccabeus was killed in battle with Bacchides (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.9.18","r":"1Macc.9.18","rawR":"1Macc.9.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.9.18","value":"1Macc.9.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 9:18"},"), his brother Jonathan became his successor (vv ",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.9.28-31","r":"1Macc.9.28-31","rawR":"1Macc.9.28-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.9.28-31","value":"1Macc.9.28-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"28-31"},"). Jonathan continued the struggle against Syria for three years with a small band of guerrillas. But the Syrians were busy with an internal struggle for political power, and so, in 157 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", made peace with him. The political machinations in Syria worked to Jonathan’s advantage, and five years later he became high priest in Jerusalem and administrator of Judea (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.10.1-11","r":"1Macc.10.1-11","rawR":"1Macc.10.1-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.10.1-11","value":"1Macc.10.1-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:1-11"},"). Under his management, Jewish territory and power increased. This occurred partly because Jonathan was able to play the Syrian political rivals against one another. One of these was Tryphon, a pretender to the Syrian throne who saw that his influence was threatened by Jonathan’s power. So in 143 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," he decided to overthrow the Jewish leader. Jonathan was taken prisoner by Tryphon through treachery and eventually killed, leaving his brother Simon to lead the Jews (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.12.1-13.53","r":"1Macc.12.1-13.53","rawR":"1Macc.12.1-13.53","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.12.1-13.53","value":"1Macc.12.1-13.53"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 12–13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Jonathan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 23:14-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.23.14-15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.23.14-15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.23.14-15"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 17:7-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.17.7-10","rawQueryValue":"Judg.17.7-10","sourceRefExact":"Judg.17.7-10"},{"anchorText":"18:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.18.30","rawQueryValue":"Judg.18.30","sourceRefExact":"Judg.18.30"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 14:49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.14.49","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.14.49","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.14.49"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 8:33-34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.33-34","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.33-34","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.33-34"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 13:2-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.13.2-4","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.13.2-4","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.13.2-4"},{"anchorText":"14:1-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.14.1-15","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.14.1-15","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.14.1-15"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 1:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.1.22","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.1.22","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.1.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 18:1-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.18.1-5","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.18.1-5","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.18.1-5"},{"anchorText":"19:1-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.19.1-7","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.19.1-7","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.19.1-7"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 31:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.31.2","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.31.2","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.31.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 10:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.10.2","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.10.2","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.10.2"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 15:27, 36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.15.27,36","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.15.27,36","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.15.27,36"},{"anchorText":"17:17, 20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.17.17,20","rawQueryVal